{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-e48c7fd3-1428-4e2d-8998-1845fca758c6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-94af83960c58f75d","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8009-si_ko20p/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8009-E001.md","content":"# Investigation: workspace-aware artifacts-only serving feasibility in the MLflow server\n\n## Description\n\nThis investigation resolves the feasibility questions that gate the implementation of workspace-aware artifacts-only serving in the MLflow tracking server. It determines whether `--artifacts-only` can be combined with `--enable-workspaces` without breaking the server initialization sequence for either flag used individually, and whether artifact requests carry enough information to resolve workspace membership. The deliverable is a findings report with a recommended implementation approach, consumed by the workspace-aware artifacts-only server implementation.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Analyze the tracking server initialization sequence for `--artifacts-only` and `--enable-workspaces` individually and combined: determine whether the workspace provider can be initialized without tracking stores and model registry stores, and what the combined initialization path must look like.\n- Determine whether artifact request paths (the `/api/2.0/mlflow/artifacts/*` endpoints and the underlying artifact store paths) include sufficient information — experiment ID or run ID — to resolve workspace membership. Cover the standard S3 artifact store layout (`{experiment_id}/{run_id}/artifacts/`) and identify limitations for non-standard artifact roots (initial implementation scope is the S3 artifact store, the standard RHOAI configuration).\n- Confirm the workspace store (`kubernetes://` URI scheme) can be consulted for experiment-to-workspace mapping without initializing tracking stores.\n- Validate the assumption that deployments that do not set `--enable-workspaces` (single-tenant deployments) retain the current artifacts-only proxy behavior when workspace flags are absent.\n- Produce a findings report with a recommended initialization and validation approach, including the fail-closed behavior when the workspace store is unreachable, and any server-side refactoring required.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Each feasibility question above is answered with a pass/fail verdict and supporting evidence (code references in the MLflow server source and/or a reproducible check).\n- A recommended initialization approach for the combined `--artifacts-only --enable-workspaces` mode is documented, covering workspace provider initialization without tracking/registry stores and the fail-closed behavior when the workspace store is unreachable.\n- An artifact path resolution strategy is documented, including documented limitations for non-standard artifact roots.\n- The findings report is delivered and reviewed by the MLflow team.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\nEnables HLR-1, HLR-2, HLR-3, HLR-4, and HLR-8 (P0/P2 workspace-aware artifacts-only server requirements): the answers determine the initialization and path-resolution approach of the server implementation.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":67376,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-85f574c21f19b836","agent_id":"a294f4e0cbc229ff0","session_id":"93c9eca1-ec44-4ff5-8343-c9e3bc7bdf0f","uuid":"7ddec5e2-e158-41a0-90d1-f1b10f550d2d","timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:35:24.756Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8009"}
