{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-7e33441c-436e-4338-8baa-c09c83b2a8f5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-82fdedf801a8cda9","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8009-si_ko20p/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8009-BRANCH-B-E007.md","content":"# Tracking server artifact traffic delegation to the dedicated artifacts-only instance\n\n## Description\n\nConditional branch (outcome B of the artifact traffic routing investigation): if gateway-level path-based routing is insufficient to route artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance, this epic implements the tracking server configuration change that delegates artifact operations to that instance. The main tracking server continues to serve experiment tracking, model registry, and prompt registry, while artifact requests are delegated to the dedicated instance where workspace validation applies. If the routing investigation finds gateway-level routing sufficient (outcome A), this epic is removed.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Implement the tracking server configuration change that delegates artifact operations to the dedicated artifacts-only instance, per the mechanism selected by the routing investigation.\n- Preserve current behavior when delegation is not configured — deployments without the split-server topology serve artifacts exactly as today.\n- Provide the configuration surface the operator uses to wire delegation when deploying the split-server topology.\n- Document the delegation mechanism and its compatibility constraints for the operator's routing configuration.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Artifact requests addressed to the main tracking server's artifact API are delegated to the dedicated artifacts-only instance and subject to workspace validation — measured by an end-to-end check that artifact traffic arrives at the dedicated instance and receives workspace-aware responses.