{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-81242dc08ff26dc3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E005\n3\ttitle: mlflow-kubernetes-plugins workspace resolution for the artifacts-only server\n4\t  context\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n6\tcomponent: MLflow\n7\tteam: MLflow Team\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E002\n12\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E002\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: If workspace resolution is coupled to the full tracking server\n16\t    initialization path, the epic expands to factoring resolution into an independent\n17\t    initialization path within the plugin per the investigation's refactoring plan;\n18\t    if uncoupled, it reduces to verification and test coverage.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 0\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: -1\n25\t  external_dependency: 0\n26\t  human_process_gates: -1\n27\t  repo_access: 0\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: Medium\n32\tai_implementability_score: 2\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\tbranch: null\n35\t---\n36\t# mlflow-kubernetes-plugins workspace resolution for the artifacts-only server context\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tThis epic verifies and extends the `mlflow-kubernetes-plugins` auth plugin so that its workspace resolution — the experiment-to-workspace mapping backed by the `kubernetes://` workspace store — functions correctly in the artifacts-only server context, where tracking stores and model registry stores are not initialized. The plugin already provides workspace resolution for the tracking server's non-artifact operations; this epic ensures the same resolution works when only the workspace provider is initialized. The scope of the work (verification vs refactoring) is determined by the plugin initialization-dependency investigation.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- Verify that the plugin's workspace resolution (experiment-to-workspace mapping via the workspace store, registered through the `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry point group and loaded by `WorkspaceStoreRegistry`) functions in a server context with no tracking or model registry stores initialized.\n45\t- If the investigation finds the resolution coupled to the full tracking server initialization path, factor workspace resolution into an independent initialization path within the plugin, preserving the tracking server's existing workspace resolution behavior.\n46\t- Add test coverage demonstrating workspace resolution from artifact request paths without tracking store initialization, covering the workspace membership allow and deny outcomes.\n47\t- Keep the kube-rbac-proxy sidecar and `--app-name kubernetes-auth` authentication setup unchanged — authentication at the ingress level works identically for the tracking server and the artifacts-only instance.\n48\t\n49\t## Acceptance Criteria\n50\t\n51\t- Workspace resolution demonstrably functions in a server context with no tracking or model registry stores initialized — measured by passing tests covering resolution from artifact request paths for both membership allow and deny outcomes.\n52\t- Any refactoring preserves the existing tracking-server workspace resolution behavior — measured by the plugin's existing test suite passing without regression.\n53\t- The authentication setup is unchanged: the plugin continues to load via `--app-name kubernetes-auth` with the kube-rbac-proxy sidecar pattern intact.\n54\t\n55\t## HLR Traceability\n56\t\n57\t- HLR-7 (P1): auth plugin workspace resolution functions correctly in the artifacts-only context without tracking store initialization — this epic.\n58\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9c859964578464b6","agent_id":"a0a6494381c67b2ac","session_id":"93c9eca1-ec44-4ff5-8