{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9eecb4e38f78a654","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-BRANCH-B-E007\n3\ttitle: Tracking server artifact traffic delegation to the dedicated artifacts-only\n4\t  instance\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n6\tcomponent: MLflow\n7\tteam: MLflow Team\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P1\n10\tbranch: B\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E003\n12\tdependencies:\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E003\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: remove\n16\t  fallback_approach: 'If gateway path-based HTTPRoute routing suffices (outcome A),\n17\t    this epic is removed: the operator''s routing configuration alone routes artifact\n18\t    traffic to the dedicated instance with no tracking-server change.'\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 0\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: -1\n25\t  external_dependency: 1\n26\t  human_process_gates: -1\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: Medium\n32\tai_implementability_score: 2\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Tracking server artifact traffic delegation to the dedicated artifacts-only instance\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tConditional branch (outcome B of the artifact traffic routing investigation): if gateway-level path-based routing is insufficient to route artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance, this epic implements the tracking server configuration change that delegates artifact operations to that instance. The main tracking server continues to serve experiment tracking, model registry, and prompt registry, while artifact requests are delegated to the dedicated instance where workspace validation applies. If the routing investigation finds gateway-level routing sufficient (outcome A), this epic is removed.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Implement the tracking server configuration change that delegates artifact operations to the dedicated artifacts-only instance, per the mechanism selected by the routing investigation.\n44\t- Preserve current behavior when delegation is not configured — deployments without the split-server topology serve artifacts exactly as today.\n45\t- Provide the configuration surface the operator uses to wire delegation when deploying the split-server topology.\n46\t- Document the delegation mechanism and its compatibility constraints for the operator's routing configuration.\n47\t\n48\t## Acceptance Criteria\n49\t\n50\t- Artifact requests addressed to the main tracking server's artifact API are delegated to the dedicated artifacts-only instance and subject to workspace validation — measured by an end-to-end check that artifact traffic arrives at the dedicated instance and receives workspace-aware responses.\n51\t- No behavior change when delegation is not configured — measured by the existing tracking server artifact-serving behavior and test suite passing unchanged.\n52\t- The delegation mechanism and its configuration surface are documented for use by the operator's split-server topology.\n53\t\n54\t## HLR Traceability\n55\t\n56\t- HLR-6 (P1): main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance — this epic covers the server-side delegation portion, conditional on the routing investigation selecting outcome B (tracking-server delegation required).\n57\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9c859964578464b6","agent_id":"a0a6494381c67b2ac","session_id":"93c9eca1-ec44-4ff5-8343-c9e3bc7bdf0f","uuid":"e5571eb1-b78f-4dae-98d7-f27269a23af8","timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:38:29.608Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9eecb4e38f78a654","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
