{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-868ffcabc3859be8","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E006\n3\ttitle: MLflow operator split-server topology for dedicated artifacts-only serving\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n5\tcomponent: MLflow\n6\tteam: MLflow Team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8009-E003\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8009-E003\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If gateway path-based routing is insufficient, the routing design\n15\t    changes to the tracking-server delegation mechanism and the conditional tracking-server\n16\t    delegation branch work activates alongside this epic's topology implementation.\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 1\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n21\t  existing_foundation: 1\n22\t  open_questions: -1\n23\t  external_dependency: 1\n24\t  human_process_gates: -1\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 1\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: High\n30\tai_implementability_score: 5\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\tbranch: null\n33\t---\n34\t# MLflow operator split-server topology for dedicated artifacts-only serving\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tThis epic extends the MLflow operator to deploy a dedicated artifacts-only MLflow instance as a separate Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute, and to configure the main tracking deployment to route artifact traffic to that dedicated instance — a split-server topology managed declaratively through a single MLflow CR. The main tracking deployment continues to handle experiment tracking, model registry, and prompt registry; the artifacts-only instance handles artifact serving with workspace validation. The routing mechanism design is determined by the artifact traffic routing investigation; this epic implements the topology using the operator's existing Helm-in-operator pattern (CR spec converted to Helm values, rendered through embedded chart templates, applied via Server-Side Apply).\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- New Helm chart templates for the artifacts-only instance's Deployment, Service, and HTTPRoute, rendered through the operator's existing embedded chart mechanism and applied via Server-Side Apply — extending the chart with a second Deployment resource without structural changes to the chart architecture.\n43\t- Propagate workspace configuration (`--enable-workspaces`, `--workspace-store-uri`, `--app-name kubernetes-auth`) to the artifacts-only instance using the same configuration mechanisms the operator already uses for the main tracking deployment.\n44\t- Configure the main tracking deployment to route artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance, per the routing mechanism selected by the routing investigation (gateway-level path-based HTTPRoute routing, and any tracking-server delegation it prescribes).\n45\t- Create Gateway API HTTPRoute resources conditionally based on runtime CRD discovery, consistent with the operator's existing pattern for optional dependencies (no HTTPRoute and no failure when Gateway API CRDs are absent).\n46\t- Operator validation that rejects MLflow CR configurations where the artifacts-only instance is enabled without the workspace flags — misconfiguration could otherwise result in artifact requests bypassing workspace validation.\n47\t- Deploy the kube-rbac-proxy sidecar on the artifacts-only instance identically to the main tracking deployment.\n48\t- Incidental documentation updates for the new CR-driven split topology that fall out of this change.\n49\t\n50\t## Acceptance Criteria\n51\t\n52\t- Given an MLflow CR with split-server artifact serving enabled, when the operator reconciles the CR, then the operator creates a dedicated artifacts-only Deployment, Service, and HTTPRoute separate from the main tracking Deployment — measured by the presence of distinct Deployment resources with the correct flag combinations.\n53\t- Given the dedicated artifacts-only instance deployed by the operator, the artifacts-only Deployment runs with `--artifacts-only --enable-workspaces --workspace-store-uri kubernetes:// --app-name kubernetes-auth --serve-artifacts` — measured by inspecting the container command in the rendered Deployment spec.\n54\t- HTTPRoute resources are created only when Gateway API CRDs are discovered at runtime; their absence does not fail reconciliation.\n55\t- The operator rejects CR configurations that enable the artifacts-only instance without the workspace flags, with a clear validation error.\n56\t- End-to-end: artifact requests routed through the split topology reach the dedicated artifacts-only instance and are workspace-validated — measured by an integration verification against a workspace-aware artifacts-only server build (the served image carrying the combined-flag capability).\n57\t\n58\t## HLR Traceability\n59\t\n60\t- HLR-5 (P1): operator deploys a dedicated artifacts-only instance as a separate Deployment with its own Service and HTTPRoute — this epic.\n61\t- HLR-6 (P1): main tracking deployment routes artifact traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance — this epic (operator-side routing configuration); the conditional tracking-server delegation portion, if required by the routing investigation outcome, is planned as a conditional branch.\n62\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9eeb4c9380911cc2","agent_id":"a902f81198ff6bddb","session_id":"93c9eca1-ec44-4ff5-8343-c9e3bc7bdf0f","uuid":"fab6ca62-2720-4524-94b9-526f6cd8bfe0","timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:41:29.793Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-868ffcabc3859be8","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8009 decomposition"}
