{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9705561f67d9a0ee","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E001\n3\ttitle: 'Investigation: workspace-aware artifacts-only serving feasibility in the MLflow\n4\t  server'\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n6\tcomponent: MLflow\n7\tteam: MLflow Team\n8\ttype: Investigation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tdependencies: []\n11\tinvestigation_signals:\n12\t  question_specificity: 1\n13\t  source_accessibility: 1\n14\t  local_runnability: 0\n15\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n16\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n17\timplementation_type: null\n18\tai_signals: null\n19\tai_implementability: Medium\n20\tai_implementability_score: 1\n21\tjira_key: null\n22\tbranch: null\n23\tgated_by: null\n24\tgate_failure_impact: null\n25\t---\n26\t# Investigation: workspace-aware artifacts-only serving feasibility in the MLflow server\n27\t\n28\t## Description\n29\t\n30\tThis investigation resolves the feasibility questions that gate the implementation of workspace-aware artifacts-only serving in the MLflow tracking server. It determines whether `--artifacts-only` can be combined with `--enable-workspaces` without breaking the server initialization sequence for either flag used individually, and whether artifact requests carry enough information to resolve workspace membership. The deliverable is a findings report with a recommended implementation approach, consumed by the workspace-aware artifacts-only server implementation.\n31\t\n32\t## Scope\n33\t\n34\t- Analyze the tracking server initialization sequence for `--artifacts-only` and `--enable-workspaces` individually and combined: determine whether the workspace provider can be initialized without tracking stores and model registry stores, and what the combined initialization path must look like.\n35\t- Determine whether artifact request paths (the `/api/2.0/mlflow/artifacts/*` endpoints and the underlying artifact store paths) include sufficient information — experiment ID or run ID — to resolve workspace membership. Cover the standard S3 artifact store layout (`{experiment_id}/{run_id}/artifacts/`) and identify limitations for non-standard artifact roots (initial implementation scope is the S3 artifact store, the standard RHOAI configuration).\n36\t- Confirm the workspace store (`kubernetes://` URI scheme) can be consulted for experiment-to-workspace mapping without initializing tracking stores.\n37\t- Validate the assumption that deployments that do not set `--enable-workspaces` (single-tenant deployments) retain the current artifacts-only proxy behavior when workspace flags are absent.\n38\t- Produce a findings report with a recommended initialization and validation approach, including the fail-closed behavior when the workspace store is unreachable, and any server-side refactoring required.\n39\t\n40\t## Acceptance Criteria\n41\t\n42\t- Each feasibility question above is answered with a pass/fail verdict and supporting evidence (code references in the MLflow server source and/or a reproducible check).\n43\t- A recommended initialization approach for the combined `--artifacts-only --enable-workspaces` mode is documented, covering workspace provider initialization without tracking/registry stores and the fail-closed behavior when the workspace store is unreachable.\n44\t- An artifact path resolution strategy is documented, including documented limitations for non-standard artifact roots.\n45\t- The findings report is delivered and reviewed by the MLflow team.\n46\t\n47\t## HLR Traceability\n48\t\n49\tEnables HLR-1, HLR-2, HLR-3, HLR-4, and HLR-8 (P0/P2 workspace-aware artifacts-only server requirements): the answers determine the initialization and path-resolution approach of the server implementation.\n50\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b619a9aaa03fbefc","agent_id":"a1478beee049b97f9","session_id":"93c9eca1-ec44-4ff5-8343-c9e3bc7bdf0f","uuid":"747be28d-a7ac-4126-bce5-cc161ed07a84","timest