{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b9ffde954ca04e84","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E002\n3\ttitle: 'Investigation: mlflow-kubernetes-plugins workspace resolution in the artifacts-only\n4\t  context'\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n6\tcomponent: MLflow\n7\tteam: MLflow Team\n8\ttype: Investigation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tdependencies: []\n11\tinvestigation_signals:\n12\t  question_specificity: 1\n13\t  source_accessibility: 1\n14\t  local_runnability: 0\n15\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n16\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n17\timplementation_type: null\n18\tai_signals: null\n19\tai_implementability: Medium\n20\tai_implementability_score: 1\n21\tjira_key: null\n22\tbranch: null\n23\tgated_by: null\n24\tgate_failure_impact: null\n25\t---\n26\t# Investigation: mlflow-kubernetes-plugins workspace resolution in the artifacts-only context\n27\t\n28\t## Description\n29\t\n30\tThis investigation determines whether the `mlflow-kubernetes-plugins` auth plugin's workspace resolution depends on tracking store availability, and scopes any refactoring needed for the plugin to function in the artifacts-only server context where tracking stores and model registry stores are not initialized. The deliverable is a findings report with the refactoring scope (or verification evidence that none is needed), consumed by the plugin workspace-resolution implementation.\n31\t\n32\t## Scope\n33\t\n34\t- Trace the plugin's workspace provider initialization path (registered through the `mlflow.workspace_provider` entry point group and loaded by `WorkspaceStoreRegistry`) to determine whether workspace resolution or experiment-to-workspace mapping requires tracking store or model registry store availability.\n35\t- If workspace resolution is coupled to the full tracking server initialization path, identify the concrete refactoring needed to factor workspace resolution into an independent initialization path within the plugin (modules touched, new initialization path, compatibility with the tracking server's existing usage).\n36\t- Confirm that the kube-rbac-proxy sidecar and `--app-name kubernetes-auth` authentication setup are unaffected in the artifacts-only context (authentication at the ingress level works identically for both server flavors).\n37\t- Produce a findings report with a refactoring scope estimate, or verification evidence that the plugin already resolves workspaces without tracking stores.\n38\t\n39\t## Acceptance Criteria\n40\t\n41\t- The initialization-dependency question is answered with a definitive verdict and supporting evidence (plugin source references and/or a reproducible check).\n42\t- If coupled: a concrete refactoring plan is documented (modules, independent initialization path, compatibility constraints). If not coupled: verification evidence demonstrates workspace resolution functioning without initialized tracking stores.\n43\t- A recommendation is delivered stating whether plugin changes are required before the server-side artifacts-only integration can proceed, and of what scope.\n44\t\n45\t## HLR Traceability\n46\t\n47\tEnables HLR-7 (P1: auth plugin workspace resolution functions correctly in the artifacts-only context without tracking store initialization), and transitively the P0 workspace-aware artifact serving requirements that build on the plugin's resolution capability.\n48\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b619a9aaa03fbefc","agent_id":"a1478beee049b97f9","session_id":"93c9eca1-ec44-4ff5-8343-c9e3bc7bdf0f","uuid":"f57e5b58-5ab5-41a0-b210-e8e835170251","timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:42:39.261Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b9ffde954ca04e84","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8009"}
