{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9754a07d7e232a7b","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8009-E003\n3\ttitle: 'Investigation: artifact traffic routing mechanism for the MLflow split-server\n4\t  topology'\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8009\n6\tcomponent: MLflow\n7\tteam: MLflow Team\n8\ttype: Investigation\n9\tpriority: P1\n10\tdependencies: []\n11\tinvestigation_signals:\n12\t  question_specificity: 1\n13\t  source_accessibility: 1\n14\t  local_runnability: 1\n15\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n16\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n17\timplementation_type: null\n18\tai_signals: null\n19\tai_implementability: Medium\n20\tai_implementability_score: 2\n21\tjira_key: null\n22\tbranch: null\n23\tgated_by: null\n24\tgate_failure_impact: null\n25\t---\n26\t# Investigation: artifact traffic routing mechanism for the MLflow split-server topology\n27\t\n28\t## Description\n29\t\n30\tThis investigation decides how the MLflow operator should configure artifact traffic routing from the main tracking deployment to the dedicated artifacts-only instance in the split-server topology. It determines whether gateway-level path-based HTTPRoute routing suffices, or whether the main tracking server requires a configuration change to delegate artifact operations to the dedicated instance. The deliverable is a decision record that shapes the operator's HTTPRoute design and determines whether a tracking-server delegation change is needed.\n31\t\n32\t## Scope\n33\t\n34\t- Evaluate gateway-level path-based routing of artifact API traffic to the dedicated artifacts-only instance via Gateway API HTTPRoute resources (host/path matching, backend references), consistent with the operator's existing conditional Gateway API integration.\n35\t- Determine whether the main tracking server needs a configuration change to delegate artifact operations to a dedicated instance, or whether routing alone suffices — based on how clients address artifact endpoints and how the tracking server serves artifacts today.\n36\t- Document the implications for HTTPRoute design and for the main tracking deployment's configuration.\n37\t- Classify the outcome into one of two bounded outcomes:\n38\t  - **Outcome A**: gateway path-based routing suffices; no tracking server change is needed.\n39\t  - **Outcome B**: a tracking-server configuration change to delegate artifact operations is required (conditional downstream work).\n40\t- Produce a decision record with the selected mechanism and its design implications.\n41\t\n42\t## Acceptance Criteria\n43\t\n44\t- The decision record answers, with evidence from the tracking server's artifact endpoint structure and client behavior, whether server-side delegation is required for artifact traffic to reach the dedicated instance.\n45\t- HTTPRoute design implications (path matching, backend targets, conditional creation based on runtime CRD discovery) are documented.\n46\t- The outcome is classified as one of the bounded outcomes, and the downstream plan is updated accordingly (operator routing design confirmed, or the conditional tracking-server delegation branch activated).\n47\t\n48\t## HLR Traceability\n49\t\n50\tEnables HLR-5 and HLR-6 (P1: operator deploys the dedicated artifacts-only instance and routes artifact traffic to it): the selected mechanism determines the routing design of the operator split-server topology work.\n51\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b619a9aaa03fbefc","agent_id":"a1478beee049b97f9","session_id":"93c9eca1-ec44-4ff5-8343-c9e3bc7bdf0f","uuid":"4783d2f4-2c76-4fda-90dd-e6e771072912","timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:42:39.891Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9754a07d7e232a7b","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8009"}
